{"id":"QB-261111-BR89","title":"Thien Di · 11/11 · Contextual differentiation, Limits & continuity +1","student":"Thien Di","questions":[{"id":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH4B-Q32","ref":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH4B-Q32","label":"1","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"Two cars are traveling along perpendicular roads, car A at $40$ mph and car B at $60$ mph. At noon, when car A reaches the intersection, car B is $90$ miles away and moving toward the intersection.\n\nAt $1$ P.M. the rate, in miles per hour, at which the distance between the cars is changing is","options":{"A":"$-68$","B":"$-4$","C":"$4$","D":"$68$"}},{"id":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH1A-Q06","ref":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH1A-Q06","label":"2","marks":1,"calculator":false,"stem":"If $f(x) = x^{3} + Ax^{2} + Bx - 3$, $f(1) = 4$ and $f(-1) = -6$, what is the value of $2A + B$?","options":{"A":"$12$","B":"$8$","C":"$0$","D":"$-2$"}},{"id":"APCALC-BARRONS27-PRACTICETEST-AB-1-MCQ-Q40","ref":"APCALC-BARRONS27-PRACTICETEST-AB-1-MCQ-Q40","label":"3","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"The hypotenuse $AB$ of a right triangle $ABC$ is 5 feet, and one leg, $AC$, is decreasing at the rate of 2 feet per second. The rate, in square feet per second, at which the area is changing when $AC=3$ is","options":{"A":"$\\frac74$","B":"$\\frac32$","C":"$-\\frac74$","D":"$-\\frac72$"}},{"id":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH1A-Q03","ref":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH1A-Q03","label":"4","marks":1,"calculator":false,"stem":"The domain of $g(x) = \\frac{\\sqrt{x-2}}{x^{2}-x}$ is","options":{"A":"all $x \\neq 0, 1$","B":"$x \\le 2, x \\neq 0, 1$","C":"$x \\ge 2$","D":"$x > 2$"}},{"id":"APCALCAB-2024INT-MCQ-Q83","ref":"APCALCAB-2024INT-MCQ-Q83","label":"5","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"A truck is traveling south toward the intersection of two roads, while a car is traveling east away from the intersection, as shown in the figure. When the truck is $50$ meters from the intersection, it is traveling toward the intersection at $15$ meters per second. At that moment, the car is $120$ meters from the intersection and traveling away from the intersection at $25$ meters per second. At what rate, in meters per second, is the distance, $h$ meters, between the two vehicles changing at that moment?","options":{"A":"$1.308$","B":"$10.000$","C":"$17.308$","D":"$28.846$"},"figures":[{"src":"data:image/png;base64,","alt":"Truck 50 m north of the intersection moving south toward it; car 120 m east of the intersection moving east; dashed hypotenuse h m between them; right angle at the intersection."}]},{"id":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH12B-Q05","ref":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH12B-Q05","label":"6","marks":9,"calculator":false,"stem":"A cube is contracting so that its surface area decreases at the constant rate of $72$ in.$^{2}$/sec. Determine how fast the volume is changing at the instant when the surface area is $54$ ft$^{2}$."},{"id":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH1B-Q01","ref":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH1B-Q01","label":"7","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"The graph of the function $f(x)=2e^{\\sin(x)}-3$ crosses the x-axis once in the interval $[0,1]$. What is the x-coordinate of this x-intercept?","options":{"A":"$0.209$","B":"$0.417$","C":"$0.552$","D":"$0.891$"}},{"id":"APCALC-BARRONS27-PRACTICETEST-AB-2-MCQ-Q08","ref":"APCALC-BARRONS27-PRACTICETEST-AB-2-MCQ-Q08","label":"8","marks":1,"calculator":false,"stem":"A point moves along the curve $y=x^2+1$ so that the $x$-coordinate is increasing at the constant rate of $\\frac32$ units per second. The rate, in units per second, at which the distance from the origin is changing when the point has coordinates $(1,2)$ is equal to","options":{"A":"$\\frac{7\\sqrt5}{10}$","B":"$\\frac{3\\sqrt5}2$","C":"$\\frac{3\\sqrt5}5$","D":"$\\frac52$"}},{"id":"APCALC-APCLASS-U2-POWER-RULE-QUIZ-Q05","ref":"APCALC-APCLASS-U2-POWER-RULE-QUIZ-Q05","label":"9","marks":1,"calculator":false,"stem":"$\\lim_{h\\to0}\\dfrac{(x+h)^2+4(x+h)-x^2-4x}{h}$ is","options":{"A":"$x^3+x^4$","B":"$x^2+4x$","C":"$2x+4$","D":"nonexistent"}},{"id":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH4A-Q31","ref":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH4A-Q31","label":"10","marks":1,"calculator":false,"stem":"A balloon is being filled with helium at the rate of $4$ ft$^3$/min. The rate, in square feet per minute, at which the surface area is increasing when the volume is $\\frac{32\\pi}{3}$ ft$^3$ is","options":{"A":"$4\\pi$","B":"$2$","C":"$4$","D":"$1$"}},{"id":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH12A-Q13a","ref":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH12A-Q13a","label":"11","marks":4,"calculator":true,"stem":"BC Only. A spherical snowball melts so that its surface area shrinks at the constant rate of $10$ square centimeters per minute.\n\nWhat is the rate of change of volume when the snowball is $12$ centimeters in diameter?"},{"id":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH4B-Q15","ref":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH4B-Q15","label":"12","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"The two tangents that can be drawn from the point $(3,5)$ to the parabola $y=x^2$ have slopes","options":{"A":"$1$ and $5$","B":"$0$ and $4$","C":"$2$ and $10$","D":"$2$ and $4$"}},{"id":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH4B-Q30","ref":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH4B-Q30","label":"13","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"A vertical circular cylinder has radius $r$ ft and height $h$ ft. If the height and radius both increase at the constant rate of $2$ ft/sec, then the rate, in square feet per second, at which the lateral surface area increases is","options":{"A":"$4\\pi r$","B":"$2\\pi(r+h)$","C":"$4\\pi(r+h)$","D":"$4\\pi h$"}},{"id":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH11B-Q24","ref":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH11B-Q24","label":"14","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"The table shows the speed of an object (in ft/sec) at certain times during a 6-second period.\n$$\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline \\text{time (sec)}&0&1&3&6\\\\\\hline \\text{speed (ft/sec)}&30&22&12&6\\\\\\hline\\end{array}$$\n\nEstimate its acceleration (in ft/sec$^2$) at $t=2$ seconds.","options":{"A":"$-10$","B":"$-6$","C":"$-5$","D":"$-\\tfrac{10}{3}$"}},{"id":"APCALCAB-DIAGNOSTIC-MCQ-Q39","ref":"APCALCAB-DIAGNOSTIC-MCQ-Q39","label":"15","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"A 26-foot ladder leans against a building. Its foot moves away at 3 ft/sec. When the foot is 10 feet from the building, its top moves down at $r$ ft/sec. Find $r$.","options":{"A":"$0.80$","B":"$1.25$","C":"$7.20$","D":"$12.50$"}},{"id":"APCALC-CED-MCQ-Q05","ref":"APCALC-CED-MCQ-Q05","label":"16","marks":1,"calculator":false,"stem":"The radius of a right circular cylinder is increasing at a rate of $2$ units per second. The height of the cylinder is decreasing at a rate of $5$ units per second. Which of the following expressions gives the rate at which the volume of the cylinder is changing with respect to time in terms of the radius $r$ and height $h$ of the cylinder? (The volume $V$ of a cylinder with radius $r$ and height $h$ is $V=\\pi r^2h$.)","options":{"A":"$-20\\pi r$","B":"$-2\\pi rh$","C":"$4\\pi rh-5\\pi r^2$","D":"$4\\pi rh+5\\pi r^2$"}}]}